+          <div className="fi-row fi-between" style={{ marginBottom: 16 }}><div className="fi-row"><Badge tone="brand">{fmt(catalogCounts.classes || 0)} CLASSES</Badge><Badge tone="brand">{fmt(catalogCounts.properties || 0)} PROPERTIES</Badge><Badge>{fmt(catalogCounts.individuals || 0)} REFERENCE RECORDS</Badge><Badge>{fmt(catalogCounts.restrictions || 0)} RESTRICTIONS</Badge></div>{sourceUrl && <NavButton href={sourceUrl} small>View pinned source ↗</NavButton>}</div>
+          <div className="fi-domain-grid">{domains.map(domain => <div className="fi-domain" key={domain.code}><strong>{domain.code} <span className="fi-muted" style={{ fontWeight: 400 }}>· {domain.label}</span></strong><div className="fi-tiny fi-muted" style={{ marginTop: 5 }}>{fmt(domain.classes || 0)} classes · {fmt(domain.properties || 0)} properties</div></div>)}</div>
+          <div className="fi-note" style={{ marginTop: 18 }}><strong>Read the coverage precisely.</strong> The catalog is an inspectable reference. The financial records exercise selected mappings and workflows. Imported OWL statements do not by themselves provide OWL inference, entailment validation or complete financial business coverage.</div>
+          {qualityIssues > 0 && <div className="fi-note amber" style={{ marginTop: 12 }}><strong>{qualityIssues} reference import issues are recorded.</strong> Review the catalog manifest before claiming complete source coverage.</div>}
+        </div>
+      </Panel>
+      <div className="fi-footnote">All business records in this lab are synthetic. Reference release: {reference.release_tag || "not loaded"}{commit ? ` · commit ${commit.slice(0, 12)}` : ""}. Live claims are read from current event identities; counts for seeded records and mappings come from the demo manifest.</div>
+    </>}
+    {compact && <div className="fi-note"><strong>{scenarios.length} guided scenarios.</strong> Explore ownership conflicts, separate voting and control, indirect economic paths, a share split, lending and review history.</div>}
+  </Frame>;
+}
